.TP
.BI "apply " "INSTANCE|PROJECT"
Update an existing cloud agent, or render for a local runtime.
.br
Without \-\-target (or with managed\-agents) this updates the existing cloud agent INSTANCE with its skills and tools; the lead's GitHub tool arrives this way when the project grants a cloud push. It needs \-\-asked, and always needs \-\-plan (QARGI_NESTED does not skip it); a local member's guard refuses it.
With \-\-target claude\-code it takes PROJECT instead of INSTANCE and needs no \-\-asked. Without \-\-approved it prints a plan token. With \-\-plan and \-\-approved it renders the project's enabled skills and tools into $QARGI_STATE/render/PROJECT/RUNTIME (claude\-code for this target), replacing the previous render atomically, and prints the exact `claude \-\-add\-dir ...` launch line (with \-\-mcp\-config and \-\-settings when the render has them). A local runtime cannot enforce role scoping, so the render is the union of the project's roles and role scoping is advisory there. Skills render under .claude/skills; tool packs render mcp.json and settings.json. Nothing is written into a repository or into ~/.claude, and members cannot write under the state's render/ directory.
The plan refuses, naming the pack and writing nothing, a skill whose SKILL.md name differs from the pack name, whose front matter is not closed or has more than one name key; a skill and a tool with the same name; and a tool allowlist name outside letters, digits, _, . and \-. Each plan stages into its own hidden directory and a lock serializes concurrent applies; the second refuses if the render changed meanwhile. The swap installs only the tree the token approved; the token also covers the file modes, which the manifest records.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-target " "TARGET"
claude\-code renders for a local session; managed\-agents (the default for apply) is the cloud update.
