.TP
.BI "verify " "NAME"
Run the project's whole test suite on the feature's head and record the result.
.br
Declared gates: the project answer gates is an ordered list of {name, command, tier} (command: a command line or a list of words, as test_command; tier: feature or release; names unique). Absent, test_command (release.test_command for a release) is run, as before. Declared, the gates run instead and test_command is not also run (a gate whose command is the same runs it): feature verify runs the gates of tier feature in order and release verify the feature tier, then the release tier, each stopping at the first failure (the rest are listed as not run). The verdict line is still 'full suite: pass|fail at SHA', and the run record and the status lines list each gate with its result. Before it starts it warns on standard error, and goes on, when another suite may be running: a whole\-suite run of the project in progress, a local run of the repository with a file changed in the last QARGI_ACTIVE_MINUTES minutes (default 10), or a tests/run.sh process in the repository (Linux). The output of the suite is kept in STATE/suite\-logs/PROJECT.feature\-NAME.log (PROJECT.release\-VERSION.log for a release; the last run of each). When the suite fails, the last lines of the output are the failing steps and tests that its report names (the FAILED: and FAIL lines of tests/run.sh; a test command that is no runner shows its last lines instead), where the runner kept the logs of the failed steps, and the path of that log.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-project " "PROJECT"
the project, instead of the one inferred from here.
.RE
