.RS
.TP
.BI "finish " "NAME"
Merge the feature into develop with \-\-no\-ff and delete it.
.br
Needs a passing whole\-suite run at the feature's head. A feature behind develop is refused (exit 1, nothing changed); when both sides changed the same files since their merge base, the message lists them and says to run qargi feature sync first. With the answer release.changelog.numbered true it also refuses a changelog with duplicate item numbers (qargi changelog renumber). Pushes develop if the repository has an origin. With the answer branches.delete_merged local+remote (default local) it also deletes the feature branch on origin when origin has it (asked live) and holds nothing the feature lacks; the plan shows it and its token covers origin's tip. The answer branches.push_features (never, when\-shared, always; default never) decides whether feature start, merge and sync push the feature branch: when\-shared only when origin already has it. A plain push, never forced. With the answer branches.push_develop false (default true) finish does not push develop either; the first line of its plan says 'will push develop to origin' or 'local only, will not push' with the reason (no origin, or the answer). A clean worktree of the feature under the worktree root is detached and removed after the merge, when the branch is deleted. It asks the live origin with git ls\-remote (QARGI_REMOTE_TIMEOUT seconds, default 10) where the branches are, not the last fetch, and says 'remote not checked' when origin cannot be reached. A merge that conflicts changes nothing: the merge is left in progress in a worktree under the state directory (exit 3), you or the lead resolve and commit it there, and the same command with \-\-resolved applies exactly that merge. It is refused first (exit 1, nothing changed) while a run prepared against feature/NAME is open, and lists each one: prepared and not verified, verified and not applied, or applied and not merged. A run that was cleaned, discarded (local clean \-\-discard), closed (local close \-\-applied\-by\-am) or applied and merged is not open.
.RS
