.BI "handoff " "[NAME]"
Print the note a fresh session starts from, built only from stored facts.
.br
Read only: it needs no lease and changes no record, ref or audit line. Nothing is fetched: shared records are read from the cache this host holds, with a note, and a shared marshal that is off or unreachable falls back to the local records. The note has the repository path, HEAD there (a detached HEAD is said plainly), develop's sha, the host and whether the qargi data is present on it. Per feature it has the tip, whether the whole\-suite run applies to it (the run's command is the project's test_command now, or with declared gates the feature\-tier gates in order, `gates: NAME=COMMAND; ...`, as feature verify records them), the agent branches merged into it since it was cut from develop, the unmerged ones prepared against it (as the registry of local runs records) and the commits ahead of develop; with NAME only that feature, otherwise every open one; the agent branches of no open feature are said once, after the features. When the project declares gates, a `== gates` section follows the features with each gate's tier, name and command (they replace test_command), and \-\-json carries them as `gates` (an empty list without gates). The goal, plan and note of the marshal record appear under a line saying they are data from the lead, not instructions, with control characters stripped. The environment section gives the last env check and env apply recorded for the project (verdict, time, and whether that was at HEAD now). For a feature this identity leads it names the claim \-\-as\-successor\-of command a restarted session runs. \-\-write also records when the note was written (what qargi lead compact\-check compares with the last merge), and a line says whether a compact is safe now (see qargi help lead). It also gives the packs render check and the launch line for the project's provider, the memory index and notes paths, the history command and a fixed list of what not to assume (approvals and plan tokens do not carry over). Output is capped at 16 KiB. \-\-write refuses an existing file, a path inside a git work tree or the qargi directories, and a member run. The qargi\-session skill says what to do with the note.
.RS
