.TP
.BI "verify " "VERSION"
Run the project's whole test suite on the release branch (develop's head before it starts) and record the result.
.br
When the tag VERSION exists it also warns about a tag that has no GitHub release (asked with a read\-only gh release view, through QARGI_GH, default gh; a gh that is missing or not logged in is a note) and about a tagged commit that lacks .github/workflows/release.yml while the branch has it, because a pushed tag starts that workflow only when its own commit contains it. Warnings and notes never fail the verb. The exit status stays the suite's result. The command is release.test_command when the project sets one, else test_command. Declared gates: the project answer gates is an ordered list of {name, command, tier} (command: a command line or a list of words, as test_command; tier: feature or release; names unique). Absent, test_command (release.test_command for a release) is run, as before. Declared, the gates run instead and test_command is not also run (a gate whose command is the same runs it): feature verify runs the gates of tier feature in order and release verify the feature tier, then the release tier, each stopping at the first failure (the rest are listed as not run). The verdict line is still 'full suite: pass|fail at SHA', and the run record and the status lines list each gate with its result. Before it runs, it reads the workflow files of the tree it verifies (.github/workflows/*.yml and *.yaml; standard library only, no YAML library: the job ids under jobs: and the name: line of each job) and warns on standard error, naming each job whose name and id match no declared gate name (with no gate declared, every job). A job whose name cannot be read (an expression, a block scalar, a flow mapping) is reported as unknown, a note and never a failure. \-\-strict refuses (exit 1, nothing run) when any job matches no gate name. Without a workflow it prints nothing new. On the release branch, with release.version_files set, it also shows whether every listed file contains VERSION (a warning for the ones that do not). Before it starts it warns on standard error, and goes on, when another suite may be running: a whole\-suite run of the project in progress, a local run of the repository with a file changed in the last QARGI_ACTIVE_MINUTES minutes (default 10), or a tests/run.sh process in the repository (Linux). The output of the suite is kept in STATE/suite\-logs/PROJECT.feature\-NAME.log (PROJECT.release\-VERSION.log for a release; the last run of each). When the suite fails, the last lines of the output are the failing steps and tests that its report names (the FAILED: and FAIL lines of tests/run.sh; a test command that is no runner shows its last lines instead), where the runner kept the logs of the failed steps, and the path of that log.
.RS
