.br
It asks the live origin with git ls\-remote (QARGI_REMOTE_TIMEOUT seconds, default 10) where the branches are, not the last fetch, and says 'remote not checked' when origin cannot be reached. When release.notes_file is set the plan reads that file and the VERSION section of CHANGELOG.md at the head of the branch and warns of the items of the section that the file does not mention (never a refusal; the plan still has its token). An item is a line at the margin that starts with \-, *, + or a number and a dot; it is mentioned when its leading `backticked term`, else its first three words, occurs in the file, ignoring case and spacing. A notes file that is not on the branch is a warning. When release.preflight is set it runs in a copy of the branch once the plan is approved, before anything is pushed; a non\-zero exit refuses. When a pull request for the branch is open already (found with gh pr list; a gh that cannot list it is caught by the refusal of gh pr create) the plan says so, nothing is opened and the result reads 'updated PR #N'; a worktree of the branch with uncommitted changes is a warning, only what is committed is pushed. When master and the branch share no history (no merge base: git would refuse to merge unrelated histories, as with a master that is one parentless snapshot commit) the plan has the line 'join the history of master': once approved, master is merged into the branch with \-s ours \-\-allow\-unrelated\-histories, in a temporary worktree, as a new commit after the version bump and before the push, so CI runs on the joined head and release finish is an ordinary \-\-no\-ff merge. The tree of the branch must be the same before and after (checked, with the parents of the commit); otherwise nothing moves and nothing is pushed. The plan token covers the join and master's head. A branch that is checked out in a worktree with uncommitted changes is refused for the join.
.RS
