.SS Review and apply
.TP
.B qargi review
Check what an agent returned and put it on a task branch.
.RS
.TP
.BI "check " "OUT"
Check what a run returned: numbered patches, messages, manifest, groups.
.br
OUT is the member's output directory (RUN_DIR/out); the patches are read from OUT/patches only, where review apply reads them. Given a run directory instead (no patches or manifest.json in it, an out directory in it), it checks RUN_DIR/out and notes that it did. Refuses a monolithic patch, a commit without a message body and a manifest that does not match the patches. A review run passes with a report.md (or PREFIXreport.md, as in a team run) that has a Findings section instead of patches. Prints OK, WARN or FAIL lines and a summary; exit 1 when any line is FAIL (warnings alone exit 0). When the run is in the lead's registry and the project declared a take\-in scrub, a series that passes is then scrubbed: the answer review.scrub (a command line or a list of words) runs in a throw\-away checkout of the applied series (the run's base commit, then every patch with git am), with the range in QARGI_SCRUB_BASE and QARGI_SCRUB_TIP, and the answer review.trailer_policy reject fails any commit whose message has a Co\-Authored\-By or Generated\-with trailer (none, the default, checks nothing). One more line says scrub: ok, or scrub: FAIL and the first lines of the output (scrub: not run when the series check failed), and a failing scrub exits 1. The checkout is a shared clone, so no branch, tag or worktree entry is made in the repository. Both answers are the run's own copy taken by local prepare; with neither set nothing changes. A member's guard refuses setting them, and a member's own check (the member mark that local run sets is in its environment) does not run the scrub: it says scrub: not run (a member's check; the lead's check runs it) and does not fail.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-empty
accept a manifest with no commits (a team member that was blocked or had nothing to change).
.RE
.RE
.RS
.TP
.BI "apply " "[RUN_DIR]"
Apply a collected, checked run to a task branch of the repository.
.br
Refuses a run applied already or closed (local close \-\-applied\-by\-am), and unless review check passes for RUN_DIR/out (warnings allowed) and local verify accepts the run (a refs\-changed result prints the diff). Creates the branch at the commit the run's base branch had when the run was prepared and applies every patch of out/patches in order with git am, in a temporary worktree of the project's repository: your checkout is never touched and no other ref changes. The committer is the one the repository has configured, else the author of the patches. The author of every applied commit is reset to the lead's: the answer git.author ('Name <email>'), else the repository's user.name and user.email (with neither, the member's author stays and the output says so); the answer review.keep_author true keeps the member's author instead. The date stays, history already applied is not rewritten, and the member's author is recorded in the ref journal and the audit log, not in the commit. It refuses a branch that exists; a patch that does not apply removes the worktree and the branch and names the patch. On success it prints the commits and the next commands, and records branch and tip in RUN_DIR/applied and the branch in the run's ref snapshot, so local clean still accepts the run. \-\-from\-saved ID applies from <state>/runs/ID instead (refused while the run directory exists): review check of the saved OUT, local verify \-\-saved ID, the registry's repository, slug and base, and the record in the saved copy, so it is applied once. When the run's project declared a take\-in scrub (review.scrub, review.trailer_policy), apply runs it too, before anything is made, unless a passing review check recorded the same series (the patches in order and the declared scrub): then it prints the one line scrub: skipped (review check passed it for this series). A series changed after the check is scrubbed again; a failing scrub (scrub: FAIL and the first lines of the output) refuses the apply and nothing is applied. The record is the lead's, in its state directory. A member's apply does not run the scrub (scrub: not run), as its check does not.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-project " "PROJECT"
the project, instead of the one inferred from here.
.RE
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-branch " "BRANCH"
the branch to create (default agent/<slug> of the run).
.RE
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-\-from\-saved " "ID"
apply the copy local verify saved of a passed run whose directory is gone (ID: qargi.XXXXXX), with the same checks.
.RE
.RE
